{
  "about": [
    "Renderer conformance corpus for any CampusOS Discord connector (T7c / case C9).",
    "Sentences come from the nine-row template table in the ChannelSummary description of",
    "contracts/api.openapi.yaml, typed out by hand -- not generated from our renderer,",
    "which would make the check circular.",
    "EXCEPTION, read this before implementing: the frozen contract specifies that",
    "{agreed_slot} is formatted in the channel's own timezone, but it does NOT specify the",
    "format. The two 'converged' cases therefore pin the REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION",
    "(groupchat/render.py): '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M %Z' for each endpoint, joined by an EN DASH",
    "(U+2013) with a space either side. That is compatibility with us, not conformance to",
    "the contract, and it is pending a decision by the CampusOS Orchestrator. Every other",
    "case is contract-derived.",
    "A connector conforms when, for every case, it produces exactly `expect_text`, or",
    "refuses to render when `expect_refused` is true. Byte equality."
  ],
